<%#
# Notice: two-factor authentication is off

Shown on «Сводка» to a super admin whose user has no two-factor authentication: the sign-in to this console is protected
by the password alone. The notice says where the second step can really be turned on: the page of two-factor authentication
of the profile in the operator app (the button opens it), and in words the way to it through the menu. That page opens
inside an account, so a super admin who is a member of none is told to add himself to one first (the form on his user card).
Nothing is forced: a super admin without it still signs in with the password. When the server has no encryption keys the
second step cannot be enabled at all, and the notice says that instead (the names of the settings for the developer are folded).

«Больше не показывать» hides the notice for this super admin only (SuperAdmin::TwoFactorNotice); his user card says it is hidden
and brings it back. It disappears by itself once the second step is on.

## Local variables:

- `super_admin`: the signed-in super admin.
%>
<% if SuperAdmin::TwoFactorNotice.visible_for?(super_admin) %>
  <% available = Chatwoot.mfa_enabled? %>
  <% account_id = available ? super_admin.accounts.order(:id).pick(:id) : nil %>
  <section class="mb-5 flex flex-col gap-2 rounded-xl bg-n-amber-2 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-n-amber-11 outline outline-1 -outline-offset-1 outline-n-amber-4" role="status" data-testid="two-factor-notice">
    <h2 class="m-0 text-heading-3 text-n-amber-11"><%= t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.title') %></h2>
    <p class="m-0"><%= t(available ? 'super_admin.two_factor.notice.how_to' : 'super_admin.two_factor.notice.unavailable') %></p>

    <% if !available %>
      <details class="text-[13px]" data-testid="two-factor-notice-developer">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-medium"><%= t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.developer') %></summary>
        <p class="m-0 mt-1"><%= t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.unavailable_details') %></p>
      </details>
    <% elsif account_id %>
      <p class="m-0 text-[13px]" data-testid="two-factor-notice-steps"><%= t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.steps') %></p>
    <% else %>
      <p class="m-0" data-testid="two-factor-notice-no-account"><%= t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.no_account') %></p>
    <% end %>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2 pt-1">
      <% if account_id %>
        <%= link_to t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.enable'), "#{app_path}/accounts/#{account_id}/profile/mfa", class: 'button button--small', data: { testid: 'two-factor-notice-enable' } %>
      <% elsif available %>
        <%= link_to t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.open_user_card'), super_admin_user_path(super_admin), class: 'button button--small' %>
      <% end %>
      <%= button_to t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.hide'), hide_super_admin_two_factor_notice_path, method: :post,
                    class: 'button button--small button--secondary', form: { class: 'm-0' }, data: { testid: 'two-factor-notice-hide' } %>
      <span class="text-xs"><%= t('super_admin.two_factor.notice.hide_hint') %></span>
    </div>
  </section>
<% end %>
